From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] shell32: Open with from rundll32 is centred and on the taskbar (5968)

A program's open of a type with no program shows Open with through
rundll32 OpenAs_RunDLL (5965). rundll32 hands its hidden window as the
owner: the dialog sat at the screen's top edge (centred on a window
nobody sees) and, owned, had no taskbar button. A hidden owner is no
owner: the dialog is centred on the screen and on the taskbar, as
Windows' is. Gate test/noassoc-gate.sh (mutant OPENWITH_HIDDEN_OWNER).
---
--- a/dlls/shell32/openwith.c
+++ b/dlls/shell32/openwith.c
@@ -480,6 +480,12 @@
     ow->big = ow_font(14);
     SetRect(&rc, 0, 0, ow_scale(420), ow_scale(520));
     AdjustWindowRectEx(&rc, WS_CAPTION | WS_SYSMENU, FALSE, WS_EX_DLGMODALFRAME);
+    /* rundll32 (OpenAs_RunDLL, a program's open of a type with no program) hands its
+     * hidden window: the dialog is then a window of its own, centred on the screen and
+     * on the taskbar, as Windows' is -- not at the corner of a window nobody sees */
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_OPENWITH_HIDDEN_OWNER
+    if (owner && !IsWindowVisible(owner)) owner = NULL;
+#endif
     if (!owner || !GetWindowRect(owner, &orc)) SystemParametersInfoW(SPI_GETWORKAREA, 0, &orc, 0);
     ow->hwnd = CreateWindowExW(WS_EX_DLGMODALFRAME, L"SGOpenWith", L"Open with", WS_POPUP | WS_CAPTION | WS_SYSMENU,
                                max(0, orc.left + (orc.right - orc.left - (rc.right - rc.left)) / 2),
